// Siegfried, Act 1: complete public-domain German and machine-assisted English working translation.
export const siegfriedAct1Scenes = [{"number":1,"originalHeading":"ERSTE SZENE","translatedHeading":"First Scene","summary":"","sections":[{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Zwangvolle Plage! Müh' ohne Zweck!","translatedTitle":"A torment! A pointless effort!","participants":["MIME","SIEGFRIED"],"sourceStartIndex":0,"sourceLineCount":74,"turns":[{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Wald. Den Vordergrund bildet ein Teil einer Felsenhöhle, die sich links tiefer nach innen zieht, nach rechts aber gegen drei Vierteile der Bühne einnimmt. Zwei natürlich gebildete Eingänge stehen dem Walde zu offen: der eine nach rechts, unmittelbar im Hintergrunde, der andere, breitere, ebenda seitwärts. An der Hinterwand, nach links zu, steht ein grosser Schmiedeherd, aus Felsstücken natürlich geformt; künstlich ist nur der grosse Blasebalg: die rohe Esse geht - ebenfalls natürlich - durch das Felsendach hinauf. Ein sehr grosser Amboss und andre Schmiedegerätschaften\nMime, Siegfried\nsitzt, als der Vorhang nach einem kurzen Orchestervorspiel aufgeht, am Ambosse und hämmert mit wachsender Unruhe an einem Schwerte: endlich hält er unmutig ein","translation":"Forest. The foreground is formed by part of a rock cave, which extends deeper into the interior on the left, but occupies about three-quarters of the stage on the right. Two naturally formed entrances open onto the forest: one to the right, immediately in the background, the other, wider, to the side in the same area. Against the rear wall, to the left, stands a large forge, naturally formed from rock fragments; only the large bellows are artificial: the rough chimney rises—also naturally—through the rock overhang. A very large anvil and other blacksmith's tools are also present.\nMime, Siegfried\nAs the curtain rises after a short orchestral prelude, he sits at the anvil, hammering with growing restlessness on a sword: finally, he reluctantly halts.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":0,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Zwangvolle Plage! Müh' ohne Zweck!\nDas beste Schwert, das je ich geschweisst,\nin der Riesen Fäusten hielte es fest;\ndoch dem ich's geschmiedet,\nder schmähliche Knabe,\ner knickt und schmeisst es entzwei,\nals schüf' ich Kindergeschmeid!","translation":"A torment! A pointless effort!\nThe best sword I have ever welded,\nIt was held fast in the giant's fists;\nbut the one I forged it for,\nthe shameful boy,\nHe snaps it and throws it in two,\nas if I were creating children's jewelry!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":3,"sourceLineCount":7},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Mime wirft das Schwert unmutig auf den Amboss, stemmt die Arme ein und blickt sinnend zu Boden","translation":"Mime angrily throws the sword onto the anvil, braces his arms, and gazes thoughtfully at the ground.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":10,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Es gibt ein Schwert,\ndas er nicht zerschwänge:\nNotungs Trümmer zertrotzt' er mir nicht,\nkönnt' ich die starken Stücke schweissen,\ndie meine Kunst nicht zu kitten weiss!\nKönnt' ich's dem Kühnen schmieden,\nmeiner Schmach erlangt' ich da Lohn!","translation":"There is a sword,\nthat he would not perish:\nHe defied me and would not destroy Nothung's ruins,\nCould I weld the strong pieces?\nwho cannot mend my art!\nIf I could forge it for the bold,\nI received my reward for my disgrace!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":11,"sourceLineCount":7},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er sinkt tiefer zurück und neigt sinnend das Haupt","translation":"He sinks back further and inclines his head thoughtfully.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":18,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Fafner, der wilde Wurm,\nlagert im finstren Wald;\nmit des furchtbaren Leibes Wucht\nder Niblungen Hort hütet er dort.\nSiegfrieds kindischer Kraft\nerläge wohl Fafners Leib:\ndes Niblungen Ring erränge er mir.\nNur ein Schwert taugt zu der Tat;\nnur Notung nützt meinem Neid,\nwenn Siegfried sehrend ihn schwingt:\nund ich kann's nicht schweissen,\nNotung, das Schwert!","translation":"Fafner, the wild worm,\ncamps in the dark forest;\nwith the terrible force of the body\nHe guards the Nibelung hoard there.\nSiegfried's childish strength\nFafner's body would probably succumb:\nMay he win the Ring of the Nibelung for me.\nOnly a sword is fit for the task;\nOnly Notung benefits my envy,\nwhen Siegfried swings it with great emotion:\nand I can't weld it,\nNothung, the sword!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":19,"sourceLineCount":12},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er hat das Schwert wieder zurechtgelegt und hämmert in höchstem Unmut daran weiter","translation":"He has readjusted the sword and continues hammering at it in utter displeasure.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":31,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Zwangvolle Plage! Müh' ohne Zweck!\nDas beste Schwert, das je ich geschweisst,\nnie taugt es je zu der einzigen Tat!\nIch tappre und hämmre nur,\nweil der Knabe es heischt:\ner knickt und schmeisst es entzwei,\nund schmäht doch, schmied' ich ihm nicht!","translation":"A torment! A pointless effort!\nThe best sword I have ever welded,\nIt is never suitable as the sole deed!\nI just grope and hammer,\nbecause the boy demands it:\nHe snaps it and throws it in two,\nAnd though he sneers, I will not forge him!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":32,"sourceLineCount":7},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er lässt den Hammer fallen\nSiegfried, in wilder Waldkleidung, mit einem silbernen Horn an einer Kette, kommt mit jähem Ungestüm aus dem Walde herein; er hat einen grossen Bären mit einen Bastseile gezäumt und treibt diesen mit lustigem Übermute gegen Mime an","translation":"He drops the hammer\nSiegfried, dressed in wild forest garb, with a silver horn on a chain, comes rushing in from the woods with sudden impetuosity; he has harnessed a large bear with a bast rope and is urging it on with merrily exuberant abandon against Mime.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":39,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Hoiho! Hoiho! Hau' ein! Hau' ein!\nFriss ihn! Friss ihn! Den Fratzenschmied!","translation":"Hoiho! Hoiho! Hit it! Hit it!\nEat him! Eat him! The face-maker!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":41,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er lacht unbändig\nMimen entsinkt vor Schreck das Schwert; er flüchtet hinter den Herd; Siegfried treibt ihm den Bären überall nach","translation":"He laughs uncontrollably\nMimen's sword fell from his grasp in terror; he fled behind the hearth; Siegfried chased the bear after him everywhere.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":43,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Fort mit dem Tier!\nWas taugt mir der Bär?","translation":"Get rid of the animal!\nHow do I like the bear?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":45,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Zu zwei komm ich,\ndich besser zu zwicken:\nBrauner, frag' nach dem Schwert!","translation":"I'll come to two,\nto pinch you better:\nBrownie, ask for the sword!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":47,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"He! Lass das Wild!\nDort liegt die Waffe:\nfertig fegt' ich sie heut'.","translation":"Hey! Leave the game alone!\nThat's where the weapon is located:\nI finished sweeping them today.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":50,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"So fährst du heute noch heil!","translation":"That way you'll drive safely today!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":53,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er löst dem Bären den Zaum und gibt ihm damit einen Schlag auf den Rücken","translation":"He unclips the bear's bridle and strikes it on the back.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":54,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Lauf', Brauner!\nDich brauch' ich nicht mehr!","translation":"Run, brownie!\nI don't need you anymore!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":55,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Der Bär läuft in den Wald zurück\nkommt zitternd hinter dem Herde hervor","translation":"The bear runs back into the forest.\nemerges trembling from behind the herd","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":57,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Wohl leid' ich's gern, erlegst du Bären:\nwas bringst du lebend die braunen heim?","translation":"I'll gladly suffer if you slay bears:\nWhy are you bringing the brown ones home alive?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":59,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"setzt sich, um sich vom Lachen zu erholen","translation":"sits down to recover from laughing","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":61,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Nach bessrem Gesellen sucht' ich,\nals daheim mir einer sitzt;\nim tiefen Walde mein Horn\nliess ich hallend da ertönen:\nob sich froh mir gesellte ein guter Freund,\ndas frug ich mit dem Getön'!\nAus dem Busche kam ein Bär,\nder hörte mir brummend zu;\ner gefiel mir besser als du,\ndoch bessre fänd' ich wohl noch!\nMit dem zähen Baste zäumt' ich ihn da,\ndich, Schelm, nach dem Schwerte zu fragen.","translation":"I was looking for a better companion,\nwhen someone is sitting at home with me;\nmy horn in the deep forest\nI let it resound loudly:\nWhether a good friend gladly joined me,\nThat's what I asked with the noise!\nA bear came out of the bushes,\nHe listened to me, grumbling;\nI liked him better than you,\nBut I think I could find something even better!\nI bridled him with the tough bast,\nTo ask you, scoundrel, about the sword.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":62,"sourceLineCount":12}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Ich schuf die Waffe scharf,","translatedTitle":"I created the weapon to be sharp,","participants":["MIME","SIEGFRIED"],"sourceStartIndex":74,"sourceLineCount":69,"turns":[{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er springt auf und geht auf den Amboss zu\nnimmt das Schwert auf, um es Siegfried zu reichen","translation":"He jumps up and walks towards the anvil.\npicks up the sword to hand it to Siegfried","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":74,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Ich schuf die Waffe scharf,\nihrer Schneide wirst du dich freun.","translation":"I created the weapon to be sharp,\nYou will be pleased with its cutting edge.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":76,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er hält das Schwert ängstlich in der Hand fest, das Siegfried ihm heftig entwindet","translation":"He clutches the sword fearfully in his hand, which Siegfried violently wrests from him.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":78,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Was frommt seine helle Schneide,\nist der Stahl nicht hart und fest!\ndas Schwert mit der Hand prüfend\nHei! Was ist das für müss'ger Tand!\nDen schwachen Stift nennst du ein Schwert?","translation":"What good is its bright edge,\nThe steel is not hard and strong!\nexamining the sword with his hand\nHey! What is this useless junk!\nYou call that weak pen a sword?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":79,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er zerschlägt es auf dem Amboss, dass die Stücken ringsum fliegen; Mime weicht erschrocken aus","translation":"He smashes it on the anvil so that pieces fly all around; Mime recoils in fear.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":84,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Da hast du die Stücken, schändlicher Stümper:\nhätt' ich am Schädel dir sie zerschlagen!\nSoll mich der Prahler länger noch prellen?\nSchwatzt mir von Riesen und rüstigen Kämpfen,\nvon kühnen Taten und tüchtiger Wehr;\nwill Waffen mir schmieden, Schwerte schaffen;\nrühmt seine Kunst,\nals könnt' er was Rechts:\nnehm' ich zur Hand nun,\nwas er gehämmert,\nmit einem Griff zergreif' ich den Quark!\nWär' mir nicht schier zu schäbig der Wicht,\nich zerschmiedet' ihn selbst mit seinem Geschmeid,\nden alten albernen Alp!\nDes Ärgers dann hätt' ich ein End'!","translation":"There you have the pieces, you disgraceful bungler:\nI would have smashed your skull!\nShould the braggart continue to cheat me?\nTell me about giants and valiant battles,\nof bold deeds and capable defense;\nwill forge weapons for me, create swords;\npraises his art,\nas if he knew anything about the law:\nI'll take it in hand now,\nwhat he hammered,\nI'll grab the quark with one swift movement!\nI wouldn't find that little scoundrel so utterly despicable,\nI forged him myself with his own jewels,\nthe old silly Alp!\nThen my trouble would be over!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":85,"sourceLineCount":15},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Siegfried wirft sich wütend auf eine Steinbank zur Seite rechts. Mime ist ihm immer vorsichtig ausgewichen","translation":"Siegfried throws himself angrily onto a stone bench to his right. Mime had always carefully avoided him.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":100,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Nun tobst du wieder wie toll:\ndein Undank, traun, ist arg!\nMach' ich dem bösen Buben\nnicht alles gleich zu best,\nwas ich ihm Gutes schuf,\nvergisst er gar zu schnell!\nWillst du denn nie gedenken,\nwas ich dich lehrt' vom Danke?\nDem sollst du willig gehorchen,\nder je sich wohl dir erwies.","translation":"Now you're running around like crazy again:\nYour ingratitude, Traun, is terrible!\nI'll do it to the bad boy\nNot everything is immediately the best.\nwhat good I did for him,\nHe forgets far too quickly!\nWill you never remember?\nWhat will I teach you about gratitude?\nYou should obey him willingly,\nwho ever proved to be good to you.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":101,"sourceLineCount":10},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Siegfried wendet sich unmutig um, mit dem Gesicht nach der Wand, so dass er Mime den Rücken kehrt","translation":"Siegfried turns around disgruntledly, facing the wall, so that he turns his back on Mime.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":111,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Das willst du wieder nicht hören!","translation":"You don't want to hear that again!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":112,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er steht verlegen; dann geht er in die Küche am Herd","translation":"He stands there awkwardly; then he goes into the kitchen to the stove.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":113,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Doch speisen magst du wohl?\nVom Spiesse bring' ich den Braten:\nversuchtest du gern den Sud?\nFür dich sott ich ihn gar.","translation":"But you do like to eat, don't you?\nI'll bring the roast from the spit:\nDid you like to try the brew?\nI wouldn't even do it for you.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":114,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er bietet Siegfried Speise hin; dieser, ohne sich umzuwenden, schmeisst ihm Topf und Braten aus der Hand","translation":"He offers Siegfried food; Siegfried, without turning around, throws the pot and roast out of his hand.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":118,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Braten briet ich mir selbst:\ndeinen Sudel sauf' allein!","translation":"I roasted the meat myself:\nDrink your swill alone!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":119,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"stellt sich empfindlich. Mit kläglich kreischender Stimme","translation":"She feigns sensitivity. Her voice is pitifully screechy.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":121,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Das ist nun der Liebe schlimmer Lohn!\nDas der Sorgen schmählicher Sold!\nAls zullendes Kind zog ich dich auf,\nwärmte mit Kleiden den kleinen Wurm:\nSpeise und Trank trug ich dir zu,\nhütete dich wie die eigne Haut.\nUnd wie du erwuchsest, wartet' ich dein;\ndein Lager schuf ich, dass leicht du schliefst.\nDir schmiedet' ich Tand und ein tönend Horn;\ndich zu erfreun, müht' ich mich froh:\nmit klugem Rate riet ich dir klug,\nmit lichtem Wissen lehrt' ich dich Witz.\nSitz' ich daheim in Fleiss und Schweiss,\nnach Herzenslust schweifst du umher:\nfür dich nur in Plage, in Pein nur für dich\nverzehr' ich mich alter, armer Zwerg!","translation":"This is the terrible reward for love!\nThat shameful pay for sorrow!\nI raised you as a fussy child,\nwarmed the little worm with clothes:\nI brought you food and drink,\nHe protected you like his own skin.\nAnd as you grew up, I waited for you;\nI created your bed so that you might sleep easily.\nI forged you trinkets and a resounding horn;\nTo bring you joy, I endeavored gladly:\nWith wise advice I gave you wise advice,\nWith enlightened knowledge I taught you wit.\nI sit at home, working hard and sweating,\nYou can roam around to your heart's content:\nOnly for you, only in torment, only for you\nI am consumed with longing, old, poor dwarf!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":122,"sourceLineCount":16},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"schluchzend","translation":"sobbing","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":138,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Und aller Lasten ist das nun mein Lohn,\ndass der hastige Knabe mich quält und hasst!","translation":"And this is now my reward for all my burdens,\nthat the hasty boy torments and hates me!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":139,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"schluchzend\nSiegfried hat sich wieder umgewendet und ruhig in Mimes Blick geforscht. Mime begegnet Siegfrieds Blick und sucht den seinigen scheu zu bergen","translation":"sobbing\nSiegfried turned back and calmly studied Mime's gaze. Mime met Siegfried's gaze and shyly sought to avert his own.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":141,"sourceLineCount":2}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Vieles lehrtest du, Mime,","translatedTitle":"You taught me many things, Mime,","participants":["SIEGFRIED","MIME"],"sourceStartIndex":143,"sourceLineCount":73,"turns":[{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Vieles lehrtest du, Mime,\nund manches lernt' ich von dir;\ndoch was du am liebsten mich lehrtest,\nzu lernen gelang mir nie:\nwie ich dich leiden könnt'.\nTrägst du mir Trank und Speise herbei,\nder Ekel speist mich allein;\nschaffst du ein leichtes Lager zum Schlaf,\nder Schlummer wird mir da schwer;\nwillst du mich weisen, witzig zu sein,\ngern bleib' ich taub und dumm.\nSeh' ich dir erst mit den Augen zu,\nzu übel erkenn' ich, was alles du tust:\nseh' ich dich stehn, gangeln und gehn,\nknicken und nicken, mit den Augen zwicken:\nbeim Genick möcht' ich den Nicker packen,\nden Garaus geben dem garst'gen Zwicker!\nSo lernt' ich, Mime, dich leiden.\nBist du nun weise, so hilf mir wissen,\nworüber umsonst ich sann:\nin den Wald lauf' ich, dich zu verlassen,\nwie kommt das, kehr ich zurück?\nAlle Tiere sind mir teurer als du:\nBaum und Vogel, die Fische im Bach,\nlieber mag ich sie leiden als dich:\nwie kommt das nun, kehr' ich zurück?\nBist du klug, so tu mir's kund.","translation":"You taught me many things, Mime,\nand I learned some things from you;\nBut what you most loved to teach me,\nI never managed to learn:\nHow I could stand you!\nWill you bring me food and drink?\nDisgust alone feeds me;\nCan you create a light camp for sleeping?\nI find it difficult to fall asleep then;\nAre you trying to show me how to be funny?\nI'd gladly remain deaf and stupid.\nIf I only see you with my eyes,\nI realize all too well what you do:\nWhen I see you standing, wandering, and walking,\nbending and nodding, squinting with the eyes:\nI'd like to grab the nitter by the neck,\nGive that nasty pince-nez a good thrashing!\nThat's how I learned to suffer from you, Mime.\nIf you are wise, then help me to know,\nwhat I pondered in vain:\nI'm running into the forest to leave you,\nHow come I'm returning?\nAll animals are more precious to me than you:\nTree and bird, the fish in the stream,\nI prefer her to you:\nHow come I'm returning?\nIf you are clever, let me know.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":143,"sourceLineCount":27},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"setzt sich in einiger Entfernung ihm traulich gegenüber","translation":"sits down some distance away, looking quite intimate.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":170,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Mein Kind, das lehrt dich kennen,\nwie lieb ich am Herzen dir lieg'.","translation":"My child, this will teach you to know you,\nHow dear I am to your heart.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":171,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"lachend","translation":"laughing","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":173,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Ich kann dich ja nicht leiden,\nvergiss das nicht so leicht!","translation":"I can't stand you,\nDon't forget that so easily!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":174,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"fährt zurück und setzt sich wieder abseits, Siegfried gegenüber","translation":"He drives back and sits off to the side again, opposite Siegfried.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":176,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Des ist deine Wildheit schuld,\ndie du, Böser, bänd'gen sollst.\nJammernd verlangen Junge\nnach ihrer Alten Nest;\nLiebe ist das Verlangen;\nso lechzest du auch nach mir,\nso liebst du auch deinen Mime,\nso musst du ihn lieben!\nWas dem Vögelein ist der Vogel,\nwenn er im Nest es nährt\neh' das flügge mag fliegen:\ndas ist dir kind'schem Spross\nder kundig sorgende Mime,\ndas muss er dir sein!","translation":"Your wildness is to blame for this.\nwhom you, evil one, are supposed to subdue.\nThe boys whine and demand\nafter their old nest;\nLove is desire;\nSo you also long for me,\nThat's how you love your mime too,\nThat's how you should love him!\nWhat is to the little bird is to the bird,\nwhen he feeds it in the nest\nbefore the fledgling may fly:\nThat's for you, childish offspring.\nthe knowledgeable and caring mime,\nHe must be yours!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":177,"sourceLineCount":14},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Ei, Mime, bist du so witzig,\nso lass mich eines noch wissen!\nEs sangen die Vöglein so selig im Lenz,\ndas eine lockte das andre:\ndu sagtest selbst,\nda ich's wissen wollt',\ndas wären Männchen und Weibchen.\nSie kosten so lieblich,\nund liessen sich nicht;\nsie bauten ein Nest\nund brüteten drin:\nda flatterte junges Geflügel auf,\nund beide pflegten der Brut.\nSo ruhten im Busch auch Rehe gepaart,\nselbst wilde Füchse und Wölfe:\nNahrung brachte zum Neste das Männchen,\ndas Weibchen säugte die Welpen.\nDa lernt' ich wohl, was Liebe sei:\nder Mutter entwandt' ich die Welpen nie.\nWo hast du nun, Mime,\ndein minniges Weibchen,\ndass ich es Mutter nenne?","translation":"Hey, Mime, you're so funny!\nSo let me know one more thing!\nThe little birds sang so blissfully in spring,\nOne attracted the other:\nYou said it yourself,\nbecause I wanted to know,'\nThose would be males and females.\nThey taste so lovely,\nand could not be resisted;\nThey built a nest\nand brooded inside:\nYoung fowl fluttered up,\nand both cared for the brood.\nDeer were also resting in pairs in the bushes,\neven wild foxes and wolves:\nThe male brought food to the nest.\nThe female was nursing the puppies.\nThat's where I learned what love is:\nI never took the puppies away from their mother.\nWhere have you now, Mime,\nyour lovely little wife,\nthat I call it mother?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":191,"sourceLineCount":22},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"ärgerlich","translation":"annoying","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":213,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Was ist dir, Tor? Ach, bist du dumm!\nBist doch weder Vogel noch Fuchs?","translation":"What's wrong, fool? Oh, you're so stupid!\nYou're neither a bird nor a fox, are you?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":214,"sourceLineCount":2}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Das zullende Kind zogest du auf,","translatedTitle":"You raised the weepy child,","participants":["SIEGFRIED","MIME"],"sourceStartIndex":216,"sourceLineCount":72,"turns":[{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Das zullende Kind zogest du auf,\nwärmtest mit Kleiden den kleinen Wurm:\nwie kam dir aber der kindische Wurm?\nDu machtest wohl gar ohne Mutter mich?","translation":"You raised the weepy child,\nYou warmed the little worm with clothes:\nBut how did you come to know that childish worm?\nYou probably made me without my mother?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":216,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"in grosser Verlegenheit","translation":"in great embarrassment","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":220,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Glauben sollst du, was ich dir sage:\nich bin dir Vater und Mutter zugleich.","translation":"You should believe what I tell you:\nI am both your father and mother.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":221,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Das lügst du, garstiger Gauch!\nWie die Jungen den Alten gleichen,\ndas hab' ich mir glücklich ersehn.\nNun kam ich zum klaren Bach:\nda erspäht' ich die Bäum' und Tier' im Spiegel;\nSonn' und Wolken, wie sie nur sind,\nim Glitzer erschienen sie gleich.\nDa sah ich denn auch mein eigen Bild;\nganz anders als du dünkt' ich mir da:\nso glich wohl der Kröte ein glänzender Fisch;\ndoch kroch nie ein Fisch aus der Kröte!","translation":"You're lying, you nasty fool!\nHow the young resemble the old,\nI was so happy to have that.\nNow I came to the clear stream:\nThere I spied the trees and animals in the mirror;\nSun and clouds, just as they are,\nThey appeared immediately, glittering.\nThen I saw my own image;\nI felt completely different from you:\nThe toad resembled a shiny fish;\nBut no fish ever crawled out of the toad!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":223,"sourceLineCount":11},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"höchst ärgerlich","translation":"extremely annoying","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":234,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Gräulichen Unsinn kramst du da aus!","translation":"You're digging up some truly awful nonsense!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":235,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"immer lebendiger","translation":"ever more lively","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":236,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Siehst du, nun fällt auch selbst mir ein,\nwas zuvor umsonst ich besann:\nwenn zum Wald ich laufe, dich zu verlassen,\nwie das kommt, kehr' ich doch heim?","translation":"You see, now even I remember,\nwhat I had previously pondered in vain:\nwhen I run to the forest to leave you,\nHow come I'm returning home?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":237,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"er springt auf","translation":"he jumps up","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":241,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Von dir erst muss ich erfahren,\nwer Vater und Mutter mir sei!","translation":"I need to hear from you first,\nWhoever my father and mother may be!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":242,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"weicht ihm aus","translation":"avoids him","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":244,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Was Vater! Was Mutter!\nMüssige Frage!","translation":"What about Father! What about Mother!\nPointless question!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":245,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"packt ihn bei der Kehle","translation":"grabs him by the throat","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":247,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"So muss ich dich fassen,\num was zu wissen:\ngutwillig erfahr' ich doch nichts!\nSo musst' ich alles ab dir trotzen:\nkaum das Reden hätt' ich erraten,\nentwandt ich's mit Gewalt nicht dem Schuft!\nHeraus damit, räudiger Kerl!\nWer ist mir Vater und Mutter?","translation":"That's how I have to grasp you,\nto know something:\nI won't learn anything if I'm not careful!\nSo I had to defy you in every way:\nI could hardly have guessed the speech,\nI didn't steal it from the scoundrel by force!\nOut with it, you mangy fellow!\nWho are my father and mother?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":248,"sourceLineCount":8},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"nachdem er mit dem Kopfe genickt und mit den Händen gewinkt, ist von Siegfried losgelassen worden","translation":"After he nodded his head and waved his hands, Siegfried was released.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":256,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Ans Leben gehst du mir schier!\nNun lass! Was zu wissen dich geizt,\nerfahr' es, ganz wie ich's weiss.\nO undankbares, arges Kind!\nJetzt hör', wofür du mich hassest!\nNicht bin ich Vater noch Vetter dir,\nund dennoch verdankst du mir dich!\nGanz fremd bist du mir, dem einzigen Freund;\naus Erbarmen allein barg ich dich hier:\nnun hab' ich lieblichen Lohn!\nWas verhofft' ich Tor mir auch Dank?\nEinst lag wimmernd ein Weib\nda draussen im wilden Wald:\nzur Höhle half ich ihr her,\nam warmen Herd sie zu hüten.\nEin Kind trug sie im Schosse;\ntraurig gebar sie's hier;\nsie wand sich hin und her,\nich half, so gut ich konnt'.\nGross war die Not! Sie starb,\ndoch Siegfried, der genas.","translation":"You're almost killing me!\nNow let it be! What you are stingy to know,\nFind out, just as I know.\nOh ungrateful, wicked child!\nNow listen to what you hate me for!\nI am neither your father nor your cousin,\nAnd yet, you owe yourself to me!\nYou are a complete stranger to me, my only friend;\nOut of mercy alone I hid you here:\nNow I have a lovely reward!\nWhat did I hope for, thanks to the idiot?\nOnce upon a time, a woman lay whimpering.\nout there in the wild forest:\nI helped her to the cave\nto watch over them by the warm hearth.\nShe was carrying a child in her lap;\nSadly, she gave birth here;\nshe wriggled back and forth,\nI helped as best I could.\nGreat was the need! She died,\nBut Siegfried, who recovered.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":257,"sourceLineCount":21},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"sinnend","translation":"pensively","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":278,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"So starb meine Mutter an mir?","translation":"So my mother died because of me?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":279,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Meinem Schutz übergab sie dich:\nich schenkt' ihn gern dem Kind.\nWas hat sich Mime gemüht,\nwas gab sich der Gute für Not!\n\"Als zullendes Kind\nzog ich dich auf....\"","translation":"She entrusted you to my protection:\nI'd gladly give it to the child.\nMime tried so hard,\nWhat a lot that poor man was!\n\"As a child\nI raised you....\"","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":280,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Mich dünkt, des gedachtest du schon!\nJetzt sag': woher heiss' ich Siegfried?","translation":"I think you've already thought of that!\nNow tell me: where did my name Siegfried come from?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":286,"sourceLineCount":2}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"So hiess mich die Mutter,","translatedTitle":"That's what my mother called me,","participants":["MIME","SIEGFRIED"],"sourceStartIndex":288,"sourceLineCount":73,"turns":[{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"So hiess mich die Mutter,\nmöcht' ich dich heissen:\nals \"Siegfried\" würdest du stark und schön.\n\"Ich wärmte mit Kleiden den kleinen Wurm....\"","translation":"That's what my mother called me,\nI would like to call you:\nAs \"Siegfried\" you would be strong and beautiful.\n\"I warmed the little worm with clothes....\"","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":288,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Nun melde, wie hiess meine Mutter?","translation":"Now tell me, what was my mother's name?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":292,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Das weiss ich wahrlich kaum!\n\"Speise und Trank trug ich dir zu....\"","translation":"I honestly don't know that!\n\"I brought you food and drink....\"","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":293,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Den Namen sollst du mir nennen!","translation":"Tell me the name!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":295,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Entfiel er mir wohl? Doch halt!\nSieglinde mochte sie heissen,\ndie dich in Sorge mir gab.\n\"Ich hütete dich wie die eigne Haut....\"","translation":"Did I forget it? Wait a minute!\nShe liked to be called Sieglinde,\nwho gave you to me in worry.\n\"I cherished you like my own skin....\"","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":296,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"immer dringender","translation":"increasingly urgent","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":300,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Dann frag' ich, wie hiess mein Vater?","translation":"Then I ask, what was my father's name?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":301,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"barsch","translation":"perch","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":302,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Den hab' ich nie gesehn.","translation":"I never saw him.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":303,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Doch die Mutter nannte den Namen?","translation":"But the mother mentioned the name?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":304,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Erschlagen sei er, das sagte sie nur;\ndich Vaterlosen befahl sie mir da.\n\"Und wie du erwuchsest, wartet' ich dein;\ndein Lager schuf ich, dass leicht du schliefst....\"","translation":"She said he had been killed;\nShe commanded me there, you fatherless one.\n\"And as you grew up, I waited for you;\nI made your bed so that you might sleep easily....\"","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":305,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Still mit dem alten Starenlied!\nSoll ich der Kunde glauben,\nhast du mir nichts gelogen,\nso lass mich Zeichen sehn!","translation":"Silence with the old starling song!\nShould I believe the customer?\nYou didn't lie to me,\nSo let me see some signs!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":309,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Was soll dir's noch bezeugen?","translation":"What further proof is it supposed to provide?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":313,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Dir glaub' ich nicht mit dem Ohr',\ndir glaub' ich nur mit dem Aug':\nwelch Zeichen zeugt für dich?","translation":"I don't believe you with my ear,\nI only believe you with my eyes:\nWhat sign testifies for you?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":314,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"holt nach einigem Besinnen die zwei Stücke eines zerschlagenen Schwerts herbei","translation":"After some reflection, he retrieves the two pieces of a shattered sword.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":317,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Das gab mir deine Mutter:\nfür Mühe, Kost und Pflege\nliess sie's als schwachen Lohn.\nSieh' her, ein zerbrochnes Schwert!\nDein Vater, sagte sie, führt' es,\nals im letzten Kampf er erlag.","translation":"Your mother gave me this:\nfor effort, food and care\nShe considered it a poor wage.\nLook, a broken sword!\n\"Your father,\" she said, \"is leading it.\"\nwhen he succumbed in the final battle.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":318,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"begeistert","translation":"enthusiastic","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":324,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Und diese Stücke sollst du mir schmieden:\ndann schwing' ich ein rechtes Schwert!\nAuf! Eile dich, Mime!\nMühe dich rasch;\nkannst du was Rechts,\nnun zeig' deine Kunst!\nTäusche mich nicht mit schlechtem Tand:\nden Trümmern allein trau' ich was zu!\nFind' ich dich faul, fügst du sie schlecht,\nflickst du mit Flausen den festen Stahl,\ndir Feigem fahr' ich zu Leib',\ndas Fegen lernst du von mir!\nDenn heute noch, schwör' ich,\nwill ich das Schwert;\ndie Waffe gewinn' ich noch heut'!","translation":"And you shall forge these pieces for me:\nThen I'll wield a real sword!\nCome on! Hurry, Mime!\nMake an effort quickly;\nCan you do something right?\nNow show us your art!\nDon't fool me with cheap trinkets:\nI believe even the ruins are capable of something!\nIf I find you lazy, you fit them poorly,\nAre you patching up solid steel with nonsense?\nI'll attack you coward,\nI'll teach you how to sweep!\nBecause even today, I swear,\nI want the sword;\nI'll win that weapon today!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":325,"sourceLineCount":15},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"erschrocken","translation":"frightened","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":340,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Was willst du noch heut' mit dem Schwert?","translation":"What do you want with the sword today?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":341,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Aus dem Wald fort in die Welt ziehn:\nnimmer kehr' ich zurück!\nWie ich froh bin, dass ich frei ward,\nnichts mich bindet und zwingt!\nMein Vater bist du nicht;\nin der Ferne bin ich heim;\ndein Herd ist nicht mein Haus,\nmeine Decke nicht dein Dach.\nWie der Fisch froh in der Flut schwimmt,\nwie der Fink frei sich davon schwingt:\nflieg' ich von hier, flute davon,\nwie der Wind übern Wald weh' ich dahin,\ndich, Mime, nie wieder zu sehn!","translation":"Leaving the forest and venturing out into the world:\nI'll never return!\nHow glad I am that I was free,\nNothing binds or compels me!\nYou are not my father;\nI am home in the distance;\nYour stove is not my house,\nMy ceiling is not your roof.\nLike a fish happily swimming in the flood,\nhow the finch soars freely away:\nIf I fly from here, I float away,\nLike the wind blowing over the forest, I drift away,\nMime, I'll never see you again!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":342,"sourceLineCount":13},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er stürmt in den Wald fort\nin höchster Angst","translation":"He storms off into the forest.\nin extreme fear","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":355,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Halte! Halte! Wohin?\nEr ruft mit der grössten Anstrengung in den Wald\nHe! Siegfried! Siegfried! He!","translation":"Stop! Stop! Where to?\nHe calls out into the forest with the greatest effort.\nHey! Siegfried! Siegfried! Hey!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":357,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er sieht dem Fortstürmenden eine Weile staunend nach; dann kehrt er in die Schmiede zurück und setzt sich hinter den Amboss","translation":"He watched the departing man in amazement for a while; then he returned to the smithy and sat down behind the anvil.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":360,"sourceLineCount":1}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Da stürmt er hin! Nun sitz' ich da:","translatedTitle":"There he rushes off! Now I'm sitting here:","participants":["MIME"],"sourceStartIndex":361,"sourceLineCount":14,"turns":[{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Da stürmt er hin! Nun sitz' ich da:\nzur alten Not hab' ich die neue;\nvernagelt bin ich nun ganz! -\nWie helf' ich mir jetzt?\nWie halt' ich ihn fest?\nWie führ' ich den Huien zu Fafners Nest?\nWie füg' ich die Stücken des tückischen Stahls?\nKeines Ofens Glut glüht mir die echten;\nkeines Zwergen Hammer zwingt mir die harten.","translation":"There he rushes off! Now I'm sitting here:\nTo the old need I have the new one;\nI'm completely nailed down now!\nHow do I help myself now?\nHow do I hold him?\nHow do I lead the hare to Fafner's nest?\nHow do I join the pieces of treacherous steel?\nNo oven's embers glow the real ones for me;\nNo dwarf's hammer forces me to use the hard ones.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":361,"sourceLineCount":9},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"grell","translation":"bright","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":370,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Des Niblungen Neid,\nNot und Schweiss nietet mir Notung nicht,\nschweisst mir das Schwert nicht zu ganz!","translation":"The Nibelung's envy\nNothung cannot rivet me, need and sweat,\nDon't weld the sword all the way through!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":371,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Mime knickt verzweifelnd auf dem Schemel hinter dem Amboss zusammen","translation":"Mime collapses in despair on the stool behind the anvil.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":374,"sourceLineCount":1}]}]},{"number":2,"originalHeading":"ZWEITE SZENE","translatedHeading":"Second Scene","summary":"","sections":[{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"tritt aus dem Wald an das hintere Tor der Höhle heran. Er trägt einen dunkelblauen, langen Mantel; einen Speer","translatedTitle":"He emerges from the woods and approaches the back gate of the cave. He wears a long, dark blue coat; he carrie","participants":["Stage direction","WANDERER","MIME"],"sourceStartIndex":0,"sourceLineCount":75,"turns":[{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Wanderer, Mime. Der Wanderer \u0005Wotan","translation":"Wanderer, Mime. The Wanderer Wotan","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":0,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"tritt aus dem Wald an das hintere Tor der Höhle heran. Er trägt einen dunkelblauen, langen Mantel; einen Speer führt er als Stab. Auf dem Haupte hat er einen grossen Hut mit breiter runder Krämpe, die über das fehlende eine Auge tief hereinhängt","translation":"He emerges from the woods and approaches the back gate of the cave. He wears a long, dark blue coat; he carries a spear as a staff. On his head he wears a large hat with a wide, round brim that hangs low over his missing eye.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":1,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Heil dir, weiser Schmied!\nDem wegmüden Gast\ngönne hold des Hauses Herd!","translation":"Hail to you, wise blacksmith!\nThe weary guest\nGrant the house's hearth graciously!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":2,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"ist erschrocken aufgefahren","translation":"jumped up in shock","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":5,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Wer ist's, der im wilden Walde mich sucht?\nWer verfolgt mich im öden Forst?","translation":"Who is it that seeks me in the wild forest?\nWho is following me in the desolate forest?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":6,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"sehr langsam, immer nur einen Schritt sich nähernd","translation":"very slowly, only approaching one step at a time.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":8,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"\"Wand'rer\" heisst mich die Welt;\nweit wandert' ich schon:\nauf der Erde Rücken rührt' ich mich viel!","translation":"The world calls me \"Wanderer\";\nI have already wandered far:\nOn my back on the earth I moved around a lot!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":9,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"So rühre dich fort\nund raste nicht hier,\nheisst dich \"Wand'rer\" die Welt!","translation":"So move away\nand don't speed here,\nThe world calls you \"Wanderer\"!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":12,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Gastlich ruht' ich bei Guten,\nGaben gönnten viele mir:\ndenn Unheil fürchtet, wer unhold ist.","translation":"I rested hospitably among good people,\nMany people bestowed gifts upon me:\nFor evil fears those who are evil.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":15,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Unheil wohnte immer bei mir:\nwillst du dem Armen es mehren?","translation":"Misfortune always resided with me:\nDo you want to increase the wealth of the poor?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":18,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"langsam immer näherschreitend","translation":"slowly but surely getting closer.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":20,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Viel erforscht' ich, erkannte viel:\nWicht'ges konnt' ich manchem künden,\nmanchem wehren, was ihn mühte:\nnagende Herzensnot.","translation":"I researched a lot, discovered a lot:\nI was able to announce important things to many,\nto defend himself against what troubled him:\ngnawing heartache.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":21,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Spürtest du klug\nund erspähtest du viel,\nhier brauch' ich nicht Spürer noch Späher.\nEinsam will ich und einzeln sein,\nLungerern lass' ich den Lauf.","translation":"Did you feel clever?\nand did you spy much,\nI don't need trackers or scouts here.\nI want to be lonely and alone,\nI'll let Lungerern have their way.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":25,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"tritt wieder etwas näher","translation":"comes a little closer again","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":30,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Mancher wähnte weise zu sein,\nnur was ihm not tat, wusste er nicht;\nwas ihm frommte, liess ich erfragen:\nlohnend lehrt' ihn mein Wort.","translation":"Some thought themselves wise,\nHe just didn't know what he needed;\nI inquired about what was beneficial to him:\nMy word taught him that it was worthwhile.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":31,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"immer ängstlicher, da er den Wanderer sich nahen sieht","translation":"He grew increasingly anxious as he saw the wanderer approaching.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":35,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Müss'ges Wissen wahren manche:\nich weiss mir grade genug;","translation":"Some people keep their knowledge to themselves:\nI know enough right now;","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":36,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Der Wanderer schreitet vollends bis an den Herd vor","translation":"The hiker proceeds all the way to the stove.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":38,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"mir genügt mein Witz,\nich will nicht mehr:\ndir Weisem weis' ich den Weg!","translation":"My joke is enough for me.\ni don't want anymore:\nI will show you the way, wise man!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":39,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"am Herd sich setzend","translation":"sitting at the stove","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":42,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Hier sitz' ich am Herd\nund setze mein Haupt\nder Wissenswette zum Pfand:\nmein Kopf ist dein,\ndu hast ihn erkiest,\nentfrägst du dir nicht,\nwas dir frommt,\nlös' ich's mit Lehren nicht ein.","translation":"Here I am, sitting at the stove.\nand set my head\nthe knowledge bet about the deposit:\nMy head is yours,\nYou chose him,\nDon't you ask yourself,\nwhat is good for you,\nI can't redeem it with teachings.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":43,"sourceLineCount":8},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"der zuletzt den Wanderer mit offenem Munde angestaunt hat, schrickt jetzt zusammen; kleinmütig für sich","translation":"The man who had just been staring at the hiker with his mouth open now shrinks back; timidly to himself.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":51,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Wie werd' ich den Lauernden los?\nVerfänglich muss ich ihn fragen.","translation":"How do I get rid of the lurking one?\nI have to ask him a tricky question.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":52,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er ermannt sich wie zu Strenge","translation":"He steels himself as if too strict","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":54,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Dein Haupt pfänd' ich für den Herd:\nnun sorg', es sinnig zu lösen!\nDrei der Fragen stell' ich mir frei.","translation":"I would pledge your head as collateral damage to the hearth:\nNow find a sensible solution!\nI'll answer three of the questions freely.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":55,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Dreimal muss ich's treffen.","translation":"I have to hit it three times.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":58,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"sammelt sich zum Nachdenken","translation":"gathers for reflection","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":59,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Du rührtest dich viel\nauf der Erde Rücken,\ndie Welt durchwandert'st du weit;\nnun sage mir schlau:\nwelches Geschlecht tagt in der Erde Tiefe?","translation":"You moved a lot\non Earth's back,\nYou travel far and wide through the world;\nNow tell me cleverly:\nWhat gender lives deep in the earth?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":60,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"In der Erde Tiefe tagen die Nibelungen:\nNibelheim ist ihr Land.\nSchwarzalben sind sie;\nSchwarz-Alberich hütet' als Herrscher sie einst!\nEines Zauberringes zwingende Kraft\nzähmt' ihm das fleissige Volk.\nReicher Schätze schimmernden Hort\nhäuften sie ihm:\nder sollte die Welt ihm gewinnen.\nZum zweiten was frägst du, Zwerg?","translation":"Deep in the earth, the Nibelungs meet:\nNibelheim is their land.\nThey are black elves;\nBlack Alberich once guarded them as ruler!\nThe compelling power of a magic ring\ntame the industrious people for him.\nRich treasures shimmering hoard\nthey heaped upon him:\nHe should win the world for him.\nSecondly, what are you asking, dwarf?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":65,"sourceLineCount":10}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Viel, Wanderer, weisst du mir","translatedTitle":"Much, wanderer, do you know me?","participants":["MIME","WANDERER"],"sourceStartIndex":75,"sourceLineCount":75,"turns":[{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"versinkt in immer tieferes Nachsinnen","translation":"sinks into ever deeper contemplation","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":75,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Viel, Wanderer, weisst du mir\naus der Erde Nabelnest;\nnun sage mir schlicht,\nwelches Geschlecht ruht auf der Erde Rücken?","translation":"Much, wanderer, do you know me?\nfrom the earth navel nest;\nNow tell me simply,\nWhich gender rests on the Earth's back?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":76,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Auf der Erde Rücken\nwuchtet der Riesen Geschlecht:\nRiesenheim ist ihr Land.\nFasolt und Fafner, der Rauhen Fürsten,\nneideten Nibelungs Macht;\nden gewaltigen Hort gewannen sie sich,\nerrangen mit ihm den Ring.\nUm den entbrannte den Brüdern Streit;\nder Fasolt fällte, als wilder Wurm\nhütet nun Fafner den Hort.\nDie dritte Frage nun droht.","translation":"On Earth's back\nThe giant's gender is immense:\nRiesenheim is their land.\nFasolt and Fafner, the Rough Princes,\nenvied the power of the Nibelung;\nThey acquired the enormous hoard,\nwon the ring with him.\nA dispute arose between the brothers over this;\nFasolt fell, like a wild worm\nFafner now guards the hoard.\nNow the third question looms.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":80,"sourceLineCount":11},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"der ganz in Träumerei entrückt ist","translation":"who is completely lost in reverie","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":91,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Viel, Wanderer, weisst du mir\nvon der Erde rauhem Rücken.\nNun sage mir wahr,\nwelches Geschlecht wohnt auf wolkigen Höh'n?","translation":"Much, wanderer, do you know me?\nfrom the earth's rough back.\nNow tell me the truth,\nWhich gender lives on cloudy heights?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":92,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Auf wolkigen Höh'n wohnen die Götter:\nWalhall heisst ihr Saal.\nLichtalben sind sie;\nLicht-Alberich, Wotan, waltet der Schar.\nAus der Welt-Esche weihlichstem Aste\nschuf er sich einen Schaft:\ndorrt der Stamm, nie verdirbt doch der Speer;\nmit seiner Spitze sperrt Wotan die Welt.\nHeil'ger Verträge Treuerunen\nschnitt in den Schaft er ein.\nDen Haft der Welt hält in der Hand,\nwer den Speer führt,\nden Wotans Faust umspannt.\nIhm neigte sich der Niblungen Heer;\nder Riesen Gezücht zähmte sein Rat:\newig gehorchen sie alle\ndes Speeres starkem Herrn.","translation":"The gods live on cloudy heights:\nTheir hall is called Valhalla.\nThey are light albums;\nLight-Alberich, Wotan, rules over the troop.\nFrom the world's most sacred branch of the ash tree\nHe created a shaft for himself:\nThough the trunk withers, the spear never perishes;\nWotan seals the world with his point.\nHoly Contracts Loyalty Runes\nHe cut into the shaft.\nHe holds the world in his hand,\nwhoever wields the spear,\nwhich encompasses Wotan's fist.\nThe Nibelung army bowed down to him;\nHis council tamed the giant brood:\nThey all obey eternally.\nthe spear's mighty lord.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":96,"sourceLineCount":17},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er stösst wie unwillkürlich mit dem Speer auf den Boden; ein leiser Donner lässt sich vernehmen, wovon Mime heftig erschrickt","translation":"He thrusts his spear at the ground as if involuntarily; a faint thunderclap can be heard, which startles Mime violently.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":113,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Nun rede, weiser Zwerg:\nwusst' ich der Fragen Rat?\nBehalte mein Haupt ich frei?","translation":"Now speak, wise dwarf:\nDid I know the answer to the questions?\nWill I keep my head free?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":114,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"nachdem er den Wanderer mit dem Speer aufmerksam beobachtet hat, gerät nun in grosse Angst, sucht verwirrt nach seinen Gerätschaften und blickt scheu zur Seite","translation":"After carefully observing the wanderer with the spear, he now becomes very frightened, searches confusedly for his equipment, and glances timidly to the side.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":117,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Fragen und Haupt hast du gelöst:\nnun, Wand'rer, geh' deines Wegs!","translation":"You have solved the questions and the main issue:\nNow, wanderer, go your way!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":118,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Was zu wissen dir frommt,\nsolltest du fragen:\nKunde verbürgte mein Kopf.\nDass du nun nicht weisst,\nwas dir nützt,\ndes fass' ich jetzt deines als Pfand.\nGastlich nicht galt mir dein Gruss,\nmein Haupt gab ich in deine Hand,\num mich des Herdes zu freun.\nNach Wettens Pflicht pfänd' ich nun dich,\nlösest du drei der Fragen nicht leicht.\nDrum frische dir, Mime, den Mut!","translation":"What is good for you to know,\nYou should ask:\nThe customer vouched for my head.\nThat you now don't know,\nwhich is of use to you,\nI'll now take yours as collateral.\nYour greeting was not meant to be hospitable to me,\nI gave my head into your hand,\nto enjoy the hearth.\nAccording to Wetten's duty, I now seize you,\nYou will not easily answer three of the questions.\nSo, Mime, take heart!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":120,"sourceLineCount":12},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"sehr schüchtern und zögernd, endlich in furchtsamer Ergebung sich fassend","translation":"very shy and hesitant, finally gathering himself in fearful submission","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":132,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Lang' schon mied ich mein Heimatland,\nlang' schon schied ich\naus der Mutter Schoss;\nmir leuchtete Wotans Auge,\nzur Höhle lugt' es herein:\nvor ihm magert mein Mutterwitz.\nDoch frommt mir's nun weise zu sein,\nWand'rer, frage denn zu!\nVielleicht glückt mir's, gezwungen\nzu lösen des Zwerges Haupt.","translation":"I have long avoided my homeland,\nI left a long time ago.\nfrom the mother's womb;\nWotan's eye shone brightly for me,\nIt peeks into the cave:\nMy wit pales in comparison to him.\nBut it now benefits me to be wise,\nWanderer, ask then!\nPerhaps I'll succeed, if forced.\nto solve the dwarf's head.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":133,"sourceLineCount":10},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"wieder gemächlich sich niederlassend","translation":"settling down again at a leisurely pace","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":143,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Nun, ehrlicher Zwerg,\nsag' mir zum ersten:\nwelches ist das Geschlecht,\ndem Wotan schlimm sich zeigte\nund das doch das liebste ihm lebt?","translation":"Well, honest dwarf,\nFirst, tell me:\nwhich is the gender,\nWotan showed himself to be terrible\nAnd yet the one he loves most is alive?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":144,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"sich ermunternd","translation":"encouraging","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":149,"sourceLineCount":1}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Wenig hört' ich von Heldensippen;","translatedTitle":"I heard little about heroic families;","participants":["MIME","WANDERER"],"sourceStartIndex":150,"sourceLineCount":74,"turns":[{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Wenig hört' ich von Heldensippen;\nder Frage doch mach' ich mich frei.\nDie Wälsungen sind das Wunschgeschlecht,\ndas Wotan zeugte und zärtlich liebte,\nzeigt' er auch Ungunst ihm.\nSiegmund und Sieglind' stammten von Wälse,\nein wild-verzweifeltes Zwillingspaar:\nSiegfried zeugten sie selbst,\nden stärksten Wälsungenspross.\nBehalt' ich, Wand'rer, zum ersten mein Haupt?","translation":"I heard little about heroic families;\nBut I will free myself from that question.\nThe Wälsungs are the desired race,\nthat Wotan fathered and tenderly loved,\nHe also shows him disfavor.\nSiegmund and Sieglind came from Wälse,\na wildly desperate pair of twins:\nSiegfried was conceived by them themselves,\nthe strongest Wälsung offspring.\nWill I, wanderer, keep my head first?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":150,"sourceLineCount":10},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"gemütlich","translation":"cozy","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":160,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Wie doch genau das Geschlecht du mir nennst:\nschlau eracht' ich dich Argen!\nDer ersten Frage wardst du frei.\nZum zweiten nun sag' mir, Zwerg:\nein weiser Niblung wahret Siegfried;\nFafner soll er ihm fällen,\ndass den Ring er erränge,\ndes Hortes Herrscher zu sein.\nWelches Schwert muss Siegfried nun schwingen,\ntaug' es zu Fafners Tod?","translation":"Exactly how you tell me the gender:\nI think you're clever, Argen!\nYou were free to answer the first question.\nSecondly, tell me, dwarf:\nA wise Nibelung protects Siegfried;\nHe is to cut down Fafner for him,\nthat he would win the ring\nto be the ruler of the hoard.\nWhich sword must Siegfried now wield?\nIs it suitable for Fafner's death?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":161,"sourceLineCount":10},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"seine gegenwärtige Lage immer mehr vergessend und von dem Gegenstande lebhaft angezogen, reibt sich vergnügt die Hände","translation":"Forgetting more and more of his present situation and vividly attracted to the object, he rubs his hands together with delight.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":171,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Notung heisst ein neidliches Schwert;\nin einer Esche Stamm stiess es Wotan:\ndem sollt' es geziemen,\nder aus dem Stamm es zög'.\nDer stärksten Helden keiner bestand's:\nSiegmund, der Kühne, konnt's allein:\nfechtend führt' er's im Streit,\nbis an Wotans Speer es zersprang.\nNun verwahrt die Stücken ein weiser Schmied;\ndenn er weiss, dass allein mit dem Wotansschwert\nein kühnes dummes Kind,\nSiegfried, den Wurm versehrt.","translation":"Nothung means envious sword;\nWotan encountered an ash tree trunk:\nIt should be fitting for him,\nthe one who drew it from the tribe.\nNone of the strongest heroes survived:\nSiegmund the Bold could do it alone:\nHe wielded it like a sword in the fight,\nuntil Wotan's spear shattered.\nNow a wise blacksmith keeps the pieces safe;\nFor he knows that only with Wotan's sword\na bold, stupid child,\nSiegfried, the worm, was injured.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":172,"sourceLineCount":12},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"ganz vergnügt","translation":"quite delighted","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":184,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Behalt' ich Zwerg auch zweitens mein Haupt?","translation":"Will I, as a dwarf, keep my head a second time around?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":185,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"lachend","translation":"laughing","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":186,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Der witzigste bist du unter den Weisen:\nwer käm' dir an Klugheit gleich?\nDoch bist du so klug,\nden kindischen Helden\nfür Zwergenzwecke zu nützen,\nmit der dritten Frage droh' ich nun!\nSag' mir, du weiser Waffenschmied:\nwer wird aus den starken Stücken\nNotung, das Schwert, wohl schweissen?","translation":"You are the funniest among the wise:\nWho could match your intelligence?\nBut are you so clever,\nthe childish hero\nto use for dwarven purposes,\nNow I threaten you with the third question!\nTell me, you wise weaponsmith:\nwho will emerge from the strong pieces\nNothung, the sword, probably weld?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":187,"sourceLineCount":9},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"fährt im höchsten Schrecken auf","translation":"In utter terror, he drives up","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":196,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Die Stücken! Das Schwert!\nO weh! Mir schwindelt!\nWas fang' ich an?\nWas fällt mir ein?\nVerfluchter Stahl, dass ich dich gestohlen!\nEr hat mich vernagelt in Pein und Not!\nMir bleibt er hart,\nich kann ihn nicht hämmern:\nNiet' und Löte lässt mich im Stich!","translation":"The pieces! The sword!\nOh dear! I feel dizzy!\nWhat do I begin with?\nWhat comes to mind?\nDamned steel, that I stole you!\nHe nailed me down in pain and distress!\nHe remains hard on me,\nI can't hammer it:\nRivet and solder are letting me down!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":197,"sourceLineCount":9},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er wirft wie sinnlos sein Gerät durcheinander und bricht in helle Verzweiflung aus","translation":"He throws his device around aimlessly and breaks down in utter despair.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":206,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Der weiseste Schmied weiss sich nicht Rat!\nWer schweisst nun das Schwert,\nschaff' ich es nicht?\nDas Wunder, wie soll ich's wissen?","translation":"Even the wisest blacksmith is at a loss!\nWho will weld the sword now?\nCan I not do it?\nThe miracle, how am I supposed to know?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":207,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"ist ruhig vom Herd aufgestanden","translation":"got up quietly from the stove","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":211,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Dreimal solltest du fragen,\ndreimal stand ich dir frei:\nnach eitlen Fernen forschtest du;\ndoch was zunächst dir sich fand,\nwas dir nützt, fiel dir nicht ein.\nNun ich's errate, wirst du verrückt:\ngewonnen hab' ich das witzige Haupt!\nJetzt, Fafners kühner Bezwinger,\nhör', verfall'ner Zwerg:\n\"Nur wer das Fürchten nie erfuhr,\nschmiedet Notung neu.\"","translation":"You should ask three times,\nI stood free for you three times:\nYou searched for vain distances;\nbut what you first found,\nYou couldn't think of anything that would benefit you.\nNow I guess you'll go crazy:\nI won the funny main prize!\nNow, Fafner's bold conqueror,\nListen, decaying dwarf:\n\"Only those who have never experienced fear,\nNothung reforges.\"","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":212,"sourceLineCount":11},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Mime starrt ihn gross an: er wendet sich zum Fortgange","translation":"Mime stares at him intently; he turns to leave.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":223,"sourceLineCount":1}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Dein weises Haupt wahre von heut':","translatedTitle":"May your wise head be true from this day forward:","participants":["WANDERER"],"sourceStartIndex":224,"sourceLineCount":4,"turns":[{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Dein weises Haupt wahre von heut':\nverfallen lass' ich es dem,\nder das Fürchten nicht gelernt!","translation":"May your wise head be true from this day forward:\nI'll let it fall into his hands,\nwho has not learned to be afraid!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":224,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er wendet sich lächelnd ab und verschwindet schnell im Walde. Mime ist wie vernichtet auf den Schemel hinter dem Amboss zurückgesunken","translation":"He turned away with a smile and quickly disappeared into the woods. Mime, slumped back onto the stool behind the anvil, looked utterly devastated.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":227,"sourceLineCount":1}]}]},{"number":3,"originalHeading":"DRITTE SZENE","translatedHeading":"Third Scene","summary":"","sections":[{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Verfluchtes Licht!","translatedTitle":"Cursed light!","participants":["MIME","SIEGFRIED"],"sourceStartIndex":0,"sourceLineCount":75,"turns":[{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"starrt grad vor sich aus in den sonnig beleuchteten Wald hinein und gerät zunehmend in heftiges Zittern","translation":"He stares straight ahead into the sunlit forest and begins to tremble violently.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":0,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Verfluchtes Licht!\nWas flammt dort die Luft?\nWas flackert und lackert,\nwas flimmert und schwirrt,\nwas schwebt dort und webt\nund wabert umher?\nDa glimmert's und glitzt's\nin der Sonne Glut!\nWas säuselt und summt\nund saust nun gar?\nEs brummt und braust\nund prasselt hieher!\nDort bricht's durch den Wald,\nwill auf mich zu!","translation":"Cursed light!\nWhat is causing the flames in the air?\nWhat flickers and glazes,\nwhat flickers and swirls,\nwhat floats there and weaves\nand wavers around.\nIt shimmers and sparkles there\nThe sun is blazing!\nWhat whispers and hums\nand is now speeding along at all?\nIt hums and roars\nand it's raining down here!\nThere it breaks through the forest,\nwants to come towards me!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":1,"sourceLineCount":14},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er bäumt sich vor Entsetzen auf","translation":"He recoils in horror","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":15,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Ein grässlicher Rachen reisst sich mir auf:\nder Wurm will mich fangen!\nFafner! Fafner!","translation":"A hideous maw opens up before me:\nThe worm wants to catch me!\nFafner! Fafner!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":16,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er sinkt laut schreiend hinter dem breiten Amboss zusammen\nbricht aus dem Waldgesträuch hervor und ruft noch hinter der Szene, während man seine Bewegung an dem zerkrachenden Gezweige des Gesträuches gewahrt","translation":"He collapses behind the wide anvil, screaming loudly.\nHe bursts out of the forest undergrowth and shouts from behind the scene, while his movement is perceived in the cracking branches of the bushes.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":19,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Heda! Du Fauler!\nBist du nun fertig!","translation":"Hey! You lazy one!\nAre you finished now?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":21,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er tritt in die Höhle herein und hält verwundert an","translation":"He enters the cave and stops in surprise.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":23,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Schnell! Wie steht's mit dem Schwert?\nWo steckt der Schmied?\nStahl er sich fort?\nHehe! Mime, du Memme!\nWo bist du? Wo birgst du dich?","translation":"Quick! What about the sword?\nWhere is the blacksmith?\nDid he steal away?\nHehe! Mime, you coward!\nWhere are you? Where are you hiding?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":24,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"mit schwacher Stimme hinter dem Amboss","translation":"in a weak voice behind the anvil","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":29,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Bist du es, Kind?\nKommst du allein?","translation":"Is that you, child?\nAre you coming alone?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":30,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"lachend","translation":"laughing","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":32,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Hinter dem Amboss?\nSag', was schufest du dort?\nSchärftest du mir das Schwert?","translation":"Behind the anvil?\nTell me, what did you create there?\nDid you sharpen my sword?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":33,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"höchst verstört und zerstreut hervorkommend","translation":"emerging highly disturbed and distracted","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":36,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Das Schwert? Das Schwert?\nWie möcht' ich's schweissen? -\n\"Nur wer das Fürchten nie erfuhr,\nschmiedet Notung neu.\"\nZu weise ward ich für solches Werk!","translation":"The sword? The sword?\nHow would I like to weld it?\n\"Only those who have never experienced fear,\nNothung reforges.\"\nI became too wise for such a task!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":37,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"heftig","translation":"violent","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":42,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Wirst du mir reden?\nSoll ich dir raten?","translation":"Will you talk to me?\nShould I give you some advice?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":43,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"wie zuvor","translation":"as before","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":45,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Wo nähm' ich redlichen Rat?\nMein weises Haupt hab' ich verwettet:","translation":"Where could I find honest advice?\nI have gambled away my wise head:","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":46,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"vor sich hin starrend","translation":"staring ahead","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":48,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"verfallen, verlor ich's an den,\n\"der das Fürchten nicht gelernt\".","translation":"I lost it to them,\n\"who has not learned to be afraid\".","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":49,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"ungestüm","translation":"impetuous","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":51,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Sind mir das Flausen?\nWillst du mir fliehn?","translation":"Are these just whims?\nAre you trying to run away from me?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":52,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"allmählich sich etwas fassend","translation":"gradually regaining some composure","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":54,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Wohl flöh' ich dem,\nder's Fürchten kennt!\nDoch das liess ich dem Kinde zu lehren!\nIch Dummer vergass, was einzig gut:\nLiebe zu mir sollt' er lernen;\ndas gelang nun leider faul!\nWie bring' ich das Fürchten ihm bei?","translation":"I will surely flee to him,\nHe who knows fear!\nBut I let the child learn that!\nI, stupid me, forgot what was the only good thing:\nHe should learn to love me;\nUnfortunately, this was achieved in a lazy manner!\nHow do I teach him to be afraid?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":55,"sourceLineCount":7},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"packt ihn","translation":"grab him","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":62,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"He! Muss ich helfen?\nWas fegtest du heut'?","translation":"Hey! Do I need to help?\nWhat did you sweep today?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":63,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Um dich nur besorgt,\nversank ich in Sinnen,\nwie ich dich Wichtiges wiese.","translation":"Just worried about you,\nI sank into my thoughts,\nhow I can show you something important.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":65,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"lachend","translation":"laughing","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":68,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Bis unter den Sitz warst du versunken:\nwas Wichtiges fandest du da?","translation":"You were sunk up to the floor beneath the seat:\nWhat important things did you find there?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":69,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"sich immer mehr fassend","translation":"increasingly taking hold","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":71,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Das Fürchten lernt' ich für dich,\ndass ich's dich Dummen lehre.","translation":"I learned to be afraid for you,\nthat I will teach you, you fool.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":72,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"mit ruhiger Verwunderung","translation":"with quiet wonder","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":74,"sourceLineCount":1}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Was ist's mit dem Fürchten?","translatedTitle":"What about the fear?","participants":["SIEGFRIED","MIME"],"sourceStartIndex":75,"sourceLineCount":75,"turns":[{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Was ist's mit dem Fürchten?","translation":"What about the fear?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":75,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Erfuhrst du's noch nie\nund willst aus dem Wald\ndoch fort in die Welt?\nWas frommte das festeste Schwert,\nblieb dir das Fürchten fern?","translation":"Have you never experienced it?\nand want to get out of the forest\nBut off into the world?\nWhat good was the sturdiest sword?\nDid you never experience fear?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":76,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"ungeduldig","translation":"impatient","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":81,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Faulen Rat erfindest du wohl?","translation":"Are you just making up bad advice?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":82,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"immer zutraulicher Siegfried näher tretend","translation":"Siegfried, becoming ever more trusting, approached.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":83,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Deiner Mutter Rat redet aus mir;\nwas ich gelobte, muss ich nun lösen:\nin die listige Welt dich nicht zu entlassen,\neh' du nicht das Fürchten gelernt.","translation":"Your mother's advice speaks through me;\nWhat I promised, I now have to deliver:\nnot to release you into the cunning world,\n'Ear, you haven't learned to be afraid.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":84,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"heftig","translation":"violent","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":88,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Ist's eine Kunst,\nwas kenn' ich sie nicht?\nHeraus! Was ist's mit dem Fürchten?","translation":"Is it an art,\nWhy don't I know them?\nCome out! What's with all the fear?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":89,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Fühltest du nie im finstren Wald,\nbei Dämmerschein am dunklen Ort,\nwenn fern es säuselt, summt und saust,\nwildes Brummen näher braust,\nwirres Flackern um dich flimmert,\nschwellend Schwirren zu Leib dir schwebt:\nfühltest du dann nicht grieselnd\nGrausen die Glieder dir fahen?\nGlühender Schauer schüttelt die Glieder,\nin der Brust bebend und bang\nberstet hämmernd das Herz?\nFühltest du das noch nicht,\ndas Fürchten blieb dir dann fremd.","translation":"Have you never felt in the dark forest,\nat dusk in a dark place,\nwhen it whispers, hums and whooshes in the distance,\nA wild buzzing sound rushes closer,\nA chaotic flickering surrounds you,\nA swelling, whirring sensation hovers around your body:\nDidn't you feel gritty then?\nDo your limbs shudder with horror?\nA burning shiver shakes the limbs,\ntrembling and anxious in my chest\nDoes the heart burst with a pounding sound?\nHaven't you felt that yet?\nFear remained foreign to you.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":92,"sourceLineCount":13},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"nachsinnend","translation":"reflective","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":105,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Sonderlich seltsam muss das sein!\nHart und fest, fühl' ich, steht mir das Herz.\nDas Grieseln und Grausen,\ndas Glühen und Schauern,\nHitzen und Schwindeln,\nHämmern und Beben:\ngern begehr' ich das Bangen,\nsehnend verlangt mich's der Lust!\nDoch wie bringst du, Mime, mir's bei?\nWie wärst du, Memme, mir Meister?","translation":"That must be particularly strange!\nMy heart feels hard and firm.\nThe tingling and the dread,\nthe glowing and shuddering,\nHot flashes and dizziness,\nHammering and trembling:\nI gladly desire the fear,\nMy desire yearns for it!\nBut how will you teach me, Mime?\nHow would you be, you coward, my master?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":106,"sourceLineCount":10},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Folge mir nur, ich führe dich wohl:\nsinnend fand ich es aus.\nIch weiss einen schlimmen Wurm,\nder würgt' und schlang schon viel:\nFafner lehrt dich das Fürchten,\nfolgst du mir zu seinem Nest.","translation":"Just follow me, I'll guide you:\nI found it thoughtfully.\nI know a nasty worm,\nHe chokes and has already swallowed a lot:\nFafner will teach you fear,\nWill you follow me to his nest?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":116,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Wo liegt er im Nest?","translation":"Where is he lying in the nest?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":122,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Neidhöhle wird es genannt:\nim Ost, am Ende des Walds.","translation":"It is called the Envy Cave:\nIn the east, at the edge of the forest.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":123,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Dann wär's nicht weit von der Welt?","translation":"Then it wouldn't be far from the world?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":125,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Bei Neidhöhle liegt sie ganz nah.","translation":"It is located very close to Neidhöhle.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":126,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Dahin denn sollst du mich führen:\nlernt' ich das Fürchten,\ndann fort in die Welt!\nDrum schnell! Schaffe das Schwert,\nin der Welt will ich es schwingen.","translation":"That is where you shall lead me:\nI learned to be afraid,\nThen off into the world!\nTherefore, quickly! Create the sword,\nI want to swing it in the world.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":127,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Das Schwert? O Not!","translation":"The sword? Oh dear!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":132,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Rasch in die Schmiede!\nWeis', was du schufst!","translation":"Hurry to the forge!\nKnow what you have created!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":133,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Verfluchter Stahl!\nZu flicken versteh' ich ihn nicht:\nden zähen Zauber\nbezwingt keines Zwergen Kraft.\nWer das Fürchten nicht kennt,\nder fänd' wohl eher die Kunst.","translation":"Cursed steel!\nI don't understand how to fix it:\nthe tenacious spell\nNo dwarf's strength can overcome it.\nHe who does not know fear,\nHe would probably find art more appealing.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":135,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Feine Finten weiss mir der Faule;\ndass er ein Stümper, sollt' er gestehn:\nnun lügt er sich listig heraus!\nHer mit den Stücken,\nfort mit dem Stümper!","translation":"The lazy man knows all the subtle tricks;\nHe should admit that he was a bungler:\nNow he's cleverly lying his way out of it!\nBring on the pieces!\nAway with the bungler!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":141,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"auf den Herd zuschreitend","translation":"walking towards the stove","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":146,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Des Vaters Stahl fügt sich wohl mir:\nich selbst schweisse das Schwert!","translation":"The father's steel probably submits to me:\nI will weld the sword myself!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":147,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er macht sich, Mimes Gerät durcheinander werfend, mit Ungestüm an die Arbeit","translation":"He throws Mime's device around and impetuously sets to work.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":149,"sourceLineCount":1}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Hättest du fleissig die Kunst gepflegt,","translatedTitle":"Had you diligently cultivated art,","participants":["MIME","SIEGFRIED"],"sourceStartIndex":150,"sourceLineCount":59,"turns":[{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Hättest du fleissig die Kunst gepflegt,\njetzt käm' dir's wahrlich zugut;\ndoch lässig warst du stets in der Lehr':\nwas willst du Rechtes nun rüsten?","translation":"Had you diligently cultivated art,\nNow would truly be to your advantage;\nBut you were always relaxed during your apprenticeship:\nWhat do you want to arm on the right now?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":150,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Was der Meister nicht kann,\nvermöcht' es der Knabe,\nhätt' er ihm immer gehorcht?","translation":"What the master cannot do,\nIf the boy could do it,\nWould he always have obeyed him?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":154,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er dreht ihm eine Nase","translation":"He sticks his tongue out at him.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":157,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Jetzt mach' dich fort,\nmisch' dich nicht drein:\nsonst fällst du mir mit ins Feuer!","translation":"Now get out of here,\nDon't interfere:\nOtherwise you'll fall into the fire with me!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":158,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er hat eine grosse Menge Kohlen auf dem Herd aufgehäuft und unterhält in einem fort die Glut, während er die Schwertstücke in den Schraubstock einspannt und sie zu Spänen zerfeilt\nder sich etwas abseits niedergesetzt hat, sieht Siegfried bei der Arbeit zu","translation":"He has piled a large amount of coal on the stove and is constantly tending the embers while he clamps the sword pieces in the vise and files them down into shavings.\nHaving sat down a little to the side, Siegfried watches him work.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":161,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Was machst du denn da?\nNimm doch die Löte:\nden Brei braut' ich schon längst.","translation":"What are you doing here?\nWhy don't you use the solder?\nI've already brewed the porridge.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":163,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Fort mit dem Brei!\nIch brauch' ihn nicht:\nMit Bappe back' ich kein Schwert!","translation":"Away with the porridge!\nI don't need him:\nI won't bake a sword with Bappe!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":166,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Du zerfeilst die Feile,\nzerreibst die Raspel:\nwie willst du den Stahl zerstampfen?","translation":"You're ruining the file,\nYou grind the rasp:\nHow do you intend to crush the steel?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":169,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Zersponnen muss ich in Späne ihn sehn:\nwas entzwei ist, zwing' ich mir so.","translation":"I must see him shredded into shavings:\nWhat's broken, I'll force myself to do.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":172,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er feilt mit grossem Eifer fort\nfür sich","translation":"He continues to file with great zeal.\nfor themselves","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":174,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Hier hilft kein Kluger,\ndas seh' ich klar:\nhier hilft dem Dummen die Dummheit allein!\nWie er sich rührt und mächtig regt!\nlhm schwindet der Stahl,\ndoch wird ihm nicht schwül!","translation":"No clever person can help here,\nI see that clearly:\nHere, stupidity alone helps the stupid!\nHow he stirs and moves so powerfully!\nThe steel is disappearing,\nBut he doesn't get sultry!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":176,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Siegfried hat das Herdfeuer zur hellsten Glut angefacht","translation":"Siegfried had stoked the hearth fire to a brilliant glow.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":182,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Nun ward ich so alt wie Höhl' und Wald,\nund hab' nicht so was geseh'n!","translation":"Now I've grown as old as the cave and the forest,\nand I didn't see anything like that!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":183,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Während Siegfried mit ungestümem Eifer fortfährt, die Schwertstücken zu zerfeilen, setzt sich Mime noch mehr beiseite","translation":"While Siegfried continues with impetuous zeal to file down the sword pieces, Mime sits even further to the side.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":185,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Mit dem Schwert gelingt's,\ndas lern' ich wohl:\nfurchtlos fegt er's zu ganz.\nDer Wand'rer wusst' es gut!\nWie berg' ich nun mein banges Haupt?\nDem kühnen Knaben verfiel's,\nlehrt' ihn nicht Fafner die Furcht!","translation":"It can be done with the sword,\nI guess I'll learn that:\nFearlessly, he sweeps it all away.\nThe wanderer knew it well!\nHow can I now hide my anxious head?\nThe bold boy was seized by it,\nDon't let Fafner teach him fear!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":186,"sourceLineCount":7},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"mit wachsender Unruhe aufspringend und sich beugend","translation":"jumping up and bending over with growing restlessness","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":193,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Doch weh' mir Armen!\nWie würgt' er den Wurm,\nerführ' er das Fürchten von ihm?\nWie erräng' er mir den Ring?\nVerfluchte Klemme!\nDa klebt' ich fest, fänd' ich nicht klugen Rat,\nwie den Furchtlosen selbst ich bezwäng'.","translation":"But woe is me, poor thing!\nHow he choked the worm,\nWould he experience fear from him?\nHow would he win the ring for me?\nDamn it!\nI'd be stuck there if I didn't find some wise advice,\nhow I will conquer even the fearless.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":194,"sourceLineCount":7},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"hat nun die Stücken zerfeilt und in einem Schmelztiegel gefangen, den er jetzt in die Herdglut stellt","translation":"He has now filed the pieces into smaller pieces and trapped them in a crucible, which he is now placing in the embers of the hearth.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":201,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"He, Mime! Geschwind!\nWie heisst das Schwert,\ndas ich in Späne zersponnen?","translation":"Hey, Mime! Quick!\nWhat is the name of the sword?\nthat I was spun into shavings?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":202,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"fährt zusammen und wendet sich zu Siegfried","translation":"He shudders and turns to Siegfried","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":205,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Notung nennt sich das neidliche Schwert:\ndeine Mutter gab mir die Mär.","translation":"Nothung is the name given to the envious sword:\nYour mother told me the story.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":206,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"nährt unter dem folgenden die Glut mit dem Blasebalg","translation":"feeds the embers below with the bellows","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":208,"sourceLineCount":1}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Notung! Notung! Neidliches Schwert!","translatedTitle":"Nothung! Nothung! Envious sword!","participants":["SIEGFRIED","MIME"],"sourceStartIndex":209,"sourceLineCount":74,"turns":[{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Notung! Notung! Neidliches Schwert!\nWas musstest du zerspringen?\nZu Spreu nun schuf ich die scharfe Pracht,\nim Tiegel brat' ich die Späne.\nHoho! Hoho! Hohei! Hohei! Hoho!\nBlase, Balg! Blase die Glut!\nWild im Walde wuchs ein Baum,\nden hab' ich im Forst gefällt:\ndie braune Esche brannt' ich zur Kohl',\nauf dem Herd nun liegt sie gehäuft.\nHoho! Hoho! Hohei! Hohei! Hoho!\nBlase, Balg! Blase die Glut!\nDes Baumes Kohle, wie brennt sie kühn;\nwie glüht sie hell und hehr!\nIn springenden Funken sprühet sie auf:\nHohei! Hohei! Hohei!\nZerschmilzt mir des Stahles Spreu.\nHoho! Hoho! Hohei! Hohei! Hoho!\nBlase, Balg! Blase die Glut!","translation":"Nothung! Nothung! Envious sword!\nWhat did you have to break?\nI turned chaff into sharp splendor,\nI fry the shavings in the pot.\nHoho! Hoho! Your Highness! Your Highness! Hoho!\nBlow, bellows! Blow the embers!\nA tree grew wild in the forest,\nI felled it in the forest:\nI burned the brown ash tree to make cabbage,\nIt now lies heaped on the stove.\nHoho! Hoho! Your Highness! Your Highness! Hoho!\nBlow, bellows! Blow the embers!\nThe tree's coal, how boldly it burns;\nHow bright and glorious it glows!\nIt bursts forth in leaping sparks:\nYour Highness! Your Highness! Your Highness!\nMelt the chaff of steel for me.\nHoho! Hoho! Your Highness! Your Highness! Hoho!\nBlow, bellows! Blow the embers!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":209,"sourceLineCount":19},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"immer für sich, entfernt sitzend","translation":"always sitting alone, far away","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":228,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Er schmiedet das Schwert,\nund Fafner fällt er:\ndas seh' ich nun sicher voraus.\nHort und Ring erringt er im Harst:\nwie erwerb' ich mir den Gewinn?\nMit Witz und List erlang' ich beides\nund berge heil mein Haupt.","translation":"He forges the sword,\nand Fafner he falls:\nI can foresee that with certainty.\nHe wins hoard and ring in the Harst:\nHow do I acquire the profit?\nWith wit and cunning I achieve both.\nand hide my head safely.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":229,"sourceLineCount":7},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"nochmals am Blasebalg","translation":"again at the bellows","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":236,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Hoho! Hoho! Hohei! Hohei! Hohei!","translation":"Hoho! Hoho! Your Highness! Your Highness! Your Highness!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":237,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"im Vordergrunde für sich","translation":"in the foreground for itself","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":238,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Rang er sich müd mit dem Wurm,\nvon der Müh' erlab' ihn ein Trunk:\naus würz'gen Säften, die ich gesammelt,\nbrau' ich den Trank für ihn;\nwenig Tropfen nur braucht er zu trinken,\nsinnenlos sinkt er in Schlaf.\nMit der eignen Waffe,\ndie er sich gewonnen,\nräum' ich ihn leicht aus dem Weg,\nerlange mir Ring und Hort.","translation":"He wrestled wearily with the worm,\nA drink will refresh him from his toil:\nfrom spicy juices that I collected,\nI'll brew the potion for him;\nHe only needs to drink a few drops.\nHe sinks into sleep without a purpose.\nUsing one's own weapon,\nwhich he won\nI can easily move him out of the way,\nObtain my ring and hoard.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":239,"sourceLineCount":10},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er reibt sich vergnügt die Hände","translation":"He rubs his hands together happily.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":249,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Hei! Weiser Wand'rer!\nDünkt' ich dich dumm?\nWie gefällt dir nun mein feiner Witz?\nFand ich mir wohl Rat und Ruh'?","translation":"Hey! Wise Wanderer!\nDid you think I was stupid?\nSo, how do you like my subtle joke?\nDid I find peace and quiet?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":250,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Notung! Notung! Neidliches Schwert!\nNun schmolz deines Stahles Spreu!\nIm eignen Schweisse schwimmst du nun.","translation":"Nothung! Nothung! Envious sword!\nNow melt the chaff of your steel!\nYou are now swimming in your own sweat.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":254,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er giesst den glühenden Inhalt des Tiegels in eine Stangenform und hält diese in die Höhe","translation":"He pours the glowing contents of the crucible into a rod-shaped mold and holds it aloft.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":257,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Bald schwing' ich dich als mein Schwert!","translation":"Soon I'll wield you as my sword!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":258,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er stösst die gefüllte Stangenform in den Wassereimer; Dampf und lautes Gezisch der Kühlung erfolgen","translation":"He pushes the filled rod mold into the bucket of water; steam and a loud hissing sound from the cooling process ensue.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":259,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"In das Wasser floss ein Feuerfluss:\ngrimmiger Zorn zischt' ihm da auf!\nWie sehrend er floss,\nin des Wassers Flut fliesst er nicht mehr.\nStarr ward er und steif,\nherrisch der harte Stahl:\nheisses Blut doch fliesst ihm bald!","translation":"A river of fire flowed into the water:\nA fierce anger hissed up at him!\nHow fiercely it flowed,\nIt no longer flows in the flood of water.\nHe became rigid and stiff,\nThe hard steel was imperious:\nHot blood, but it will soon flow from him!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":260,"sourceLineCount":7},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er stösst den Stahl in die Herdglut und zieht die Blasebälge mächtig an","translation":"He thrusts the steel into the embers of the hearth and pulls the bellows hard.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":267,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Nun schwitze noch einmal,\ndass ich dich schweisse,\nNotung, neidliches Schwert!","translation":"Now sweat again,\nthat I weld you,\nNothung, envious sword!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":268,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Mime ist vergnügt aufgesprungen; er holt verschiedene Gefässe hervor, schüttet aus ihnen Gewürz und Kräuter in einen Kochtopf und sucht, diesen auf dem Herd anzubringen. Siegfried beobachtet während der Arbeit Mime, welcher vom andern Ende des Herdes her seinen Topf sorgsam an die Glut stellt","translation":"Mime jumped up gleefully; he fetched various vessels, poured spices and herbs from them into a cooking pot, and tried to place it on the stove. Siegfried watched Mime as he worked, carefully positioning his pot against the embers from the other end of the stove.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":271,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Was schafft der Tölpel\ndort mit dem Topf?\nBrenn' ich hier Stahl,\nbraust du dort Sudel?","translation":"What can the fool do?\nThere with the pot?\nI'm burning steel here,\nAre you brewing smut there?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":272,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Zuschanden kam ein Schmied,\nden Lehrer sein Knabe lehrt:\nmit der Kunst nun ist's beim Alten aus,\nals Koch dient er dem Kind.\nBrennt es das Eisen zu Brei,\naus Eiern braut der Alte ihm Sud.","translation":"A blacksmith was disgraced,\nthe teacher teaches his boy:\nWith art, things are back to normal now.\nHe serves the child as a cook.\nDoes it burn the iron to a pulp?\nThe old man brews his broth from eggs.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":276,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"er fährt fort zu kochen","translation":"he continues to cook","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":282,"sourceLineCount":1}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Mime, der Künstler,","translatedTitle":"Mime, the artist,","participants":["SIEGFRIED","MIME"],"sourceStartIndex":283,"sourceLineCount":71,"turns":[{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Mime, der Künstler,\nlernt jetzt kochen;\ndas Schmieden schmeckt ihm nicht mehr.\nSeine Schwerter alle hab' ich zerschmissen;\nwas er kocht, ich kost' es ihm nicht!","translation":"Mime, the artist,\nLearn to cook now;\nHe no longer enjoys blacksmithing.\nI have shattered all his swords;\nWhatever he cooks, I won't taste it for him!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":283,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Unter dem Folgenden zieht Siegfried die Stangenform aus der Glut, zerschlägt sie und legt den glühenden Stahl auf dem Amboss zurecht","translation":"Siegfried then pulls the rod form from the embers, smashes it, and arranges the glowing steel on the anvil.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":288,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Das Fürchten zu lernen,\nwill er mich führen;\nein Ferner soll es mich lehren:\nwas am besten er kann,\nmir bringt er's nicht bei:\nals Stümper besteht er in allem!","translation":"To learn to be afraid,\ndoes he want to lead me?\nFurthermore, it should teach me:\nwhat he does best\nHe can't teach me:\nDespite being a complete amateur, he excels at everything!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":289,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"während des Schmiedens","translation":"during the forging process","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":295,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Hoho! Hoho! Hohei!\nSchmiede, mein Hammer, ein hartes Schwert!\nHoho! Hahei! Hoho! Hahei!\nEinst färbte Blut dein falbes Blau;\nsein rotes Rieseln rötete dich:\nkalt lachtest du da,\ndas warme lecktest du kühl!\nHeiaho! Haha! Haheiaha!\nNun hat die Glut dich rot geglüht;\ndeine weiche Härte dem Hammer weicht:\nzornig sprühst du mir Funken,\ndass ich dich Spröden gezähmt!\nHeiaho! Heiaho! Heiahohoho! Hahei!","translation":"Hoho! Hoho! Your Highness!\nSmith, my hammer, a hard sword!\nHoho! Hahei! Hoho! Hahei!\nOnce blood stained your pale blue;\nIts red dusting made you blush:\nYou laughed coldly there,\nYou licked the warm thing cool!\nHeiaho! Haha! Haheiaha!\nNow the embers have made you glow red;\nYour soft hardness gives way to the hammer:\nYou angrily spray me with sparks,\nthat I tamed you, you brittle one!\nHeiaho! Heiaho! Heiahohoho! Hahey!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":296,"sourceLineCount":13},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"beiseite","translation":"aside","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":309,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Er schafft sich ein scharfes Schwert,\nFafner zu fällen, der Zwerge Feind:\nich braut' ein Truggetränk,\nSiegfried zu fangen, dem Fafner fiel.\nGelingen muss mir die List;\nlachen muss mir der Lohn!","translation":"He creates himself a sharp sword,\nTo fell Fafner, the enemy of the dwarves:\nI'm brewing a deceptive drink,\nSiegfried was captured, and Fafner fell.\nThe trick must succeed for me;\nMy pay should make me laugh!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":310,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er beschäftigt sich während des folgenden damit, den Inhalt des Topfes in eine Flasche zu giessen","translation":"He then spends the next few minutes pouring the contents of the pot into a bottle.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":316,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Hoho! Hoho! Hahei!\nSchmiede, mein Hammer, ein hartes Schwert!\nHoho! Hahei! Hahei! Hoho!\nDer frohen Funken wie freu' ich mich;\nes ziert den Kühnen des Zornes Kraft:\nlustig lachst du mich an,\nstellst du auch grimm dich und gram!\nHeiaho, haha, haheiaha!\nDurch Glut und Hammer glückt' es mir;\nmit starken Schlägen streckt' ich dich:\nnun schwinde die rote Scham;\nwerde kalt und hart, wie du kannst.\nHeiaho! Heiaho! Heiahohoho! Heiah!","translation":"Hoho! Hoho! Hahei!\nSmith, my hammer, a hard sword!\nHoho! Hahei! Hahei! Hoho!\nHow I rejoice at the joyful spark!\nIt adorns the bold with the power of wrath:\nYou smile at me in a funny way,\nAre you also angry and gloating?\nHeiaho, haha, haheiaha!\nI succeeded through fire and hammer;\nI stretched you with strong blows:\nNow let the red shame fade;\nBecome as cold and hard as you can.\nHeiaho! Heiaho! Heiahohoho! Hey!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":317,"sourceLineCount":13},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er schwingt den Stahl und stösst ihn in den Wassereimer. Er lacht bei dem Gezisch laut auf. Während Siegfried die geschmiedete Schwertklinge in dem Griffhefte befestigt, treibt sich Mime mit der Flasche im Vordergrunde umher","translation":"He swings the steel and plunges it into the bucket of water. He laughs loudly at the hissing sound. While Siegfried fastens the forged sword blade into the hilt, Mime wanders around in the foreground with the bottle.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":330,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Den der Bruder schuf,\nden schimmernden Reif,\nin den er gezaubert zwingende Kraft,\ndas helle Gold, das zum Herrscher macht,\nihn hab' ich gewonnen!\nIch walte sein!","translation":"The one the brother created\nthe shimmering frost,\ninto which he conjured compelling power,\nthe bright gold that makes one a ruler,\nI won him!\nI will rule!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":331,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er trippelt, während Siegfried mit dem kleinen Hammer arbeitet und schleift und feilt, mit zunehmender Vergnügtheit lebhaft umher","translation":"He tiptoes around with increasing delight while Siegfried works with the small hammer, grinding and filing.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":337,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"Alberich selbst, der einst mich band,\nzur Zwergenfrone zwing' ich ihn nun;\nals Niblungenfürst fahr' ich darnieder;\ngehorchen soll mir alles Heer!\nDer verachtete Zwerg, wie wird er geehrt!\nZu dem Horte hin drängt sich Gott und Held:","translation":"Alberich himself, who once bound me,\nI will now force him to dwarfish toil;\nI descend as a prince of the Nibelungs;\nAll the army shall obey me!\nThe despised dwarf, how he is honored!\nGod and hero press towards the hoard:","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":338,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"mit immer lebhafteren Gebärden","translation":"with increasingly lively gestures","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":344,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"MIME","speakerTranslation":"MIME","original":"vor meinem Nicken neigt sich die Welt,\nvor meinem Zorne zittert sie hin!\nDann wahrlich müht sich Mime nicht mehr:\nihm schaffen andre den ew'gen Schatz.\nMime, der kühne, Mime ist König,\nFürst der Alben, Walter des Alls!\nHei, Mime! Wie glückte dir das!\nWer hätte wohl das gedacht?","translation":"Before my nod, the world tilts,\nShe trembles before my anger!\nThen Mime truly makes no more effort:\nOthers will create the eternal treasure for him.\nMime the bold, Mime is king,\nPrince of the Albs, Walter of the Universe!\nHey, Mime! How did you manage that!\nWho would have thought it?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":345,"sourceLineCount":8},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"hat während der letzten Absätze von Mimes Lied mit den letzten Schlägen die Nieten des Griffheftes geglättet und fasst nun das Schwert","translation":"During the last verses of Mime's song, he smoothed the rivets of the hilt with the final blows and now grasps the sword.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":353,"sourceLineCount":1}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Notung! Notung! Neidliches Schwert!","translatedTitle":"Nothung! Nothung! Envious sword!","participants":["SIEGFRIED"],"sourceStartIndex":354,"sourceLineCount":19,"turns":[{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Notung! Notung! Neidliches Schwert!\nJetzt haftest du wieder im Heft.\nWarst du entzwei, ich zwang dich zu ganz;\nkein Schlag soll nun dich mehr zerschlagen.\nDem sterbenden Vater zersprang der Stahl,\nder lebende Sohn schuf ihn neu:\nnun lacht ihm sein heller Schein,\nseine Schärfe schneidet ihm hart.","translation":"Nothung! Nothung! Envious sword!\nNow you're stuck in the book again.\nIf you were torn apart, I forced you to be whole;\nNo blow shall ever break you again.\nThe steel shattered as the dying father died.\nThe living son recreated him:\nnow his bright light smiles upon him,\nIts sharpness cuts him hard.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":354,"sourceLineCount":8},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"das Schwert vor sich schwingend","translation":"swinging his sword in front of him","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":362,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Notung! Notung! Neidliches Schwert!\nZum Leben weckt' ich dich wieder,\ntot lagst du in Trümmern dort,\njetzt leuchtest du trotzig und hehr!\nZeige den Schächern nun deinen Schein!\nSchlage den Falschen, fälle den Schelm!\nSchau, Mime, du Schmied:","translation":"Nothung! Nothung! Envious sword!\nI woke you back to life,\nYou lay dead there in the ruins,\nNow you shine defiantly and gloriously!\nShow the thieves your money now!\nStrike the wrong person, kill the scoundrel!\nLook, Mime, you blacksmith:","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":363,"sourceLineCount":7},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"er holt mit dem Schwert aus","translation":"He raises his sword","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":370,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"so schneidet Siegfrieds Schwert!","translation":"That's how Siegfried's sword cuts!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":371,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er schlägt auf den Amboss, welcher von oben bis unten in zwei Stücke zerspaltet, so dass er unter grossem Gepolter auseinander fällt. Mime, welcher in höchster Verzückung sich auf einen Schemel geschwungen hatte, fällt vor Schreck sitzlings zu Boden. Siegfried hält jauchzend das Schwert in die Höhe. Der Vorhang fällt","translation":"He strikes the anvil, which splits in two from top to bottom, falling apart with a great crash. Mime, who had been soaring onto a stool in rapture, falls to the ground in shock. Siegfried, shouting with joy, holds his sword aloft. The curtain falls.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":372,"sourceLineCount":1}]}]}];
